  - "directed-rounding interval arithmetic"
  - "integer argument principle"
  - "continuum Lipschitz certification"
abstract: >-
  We prove that the transverse Wronskian W(d,t) = (1/2) d/dd |Xi(t-id)|^2 of Riemann's
  completed Xi-function satisfies odd transverse parity W(-d,t) = -W(d,t) with identically
  vanishing even derivatives d^{2k}W/dd^{2k}(0,t) = 0, so that the parity-reduced Wronskian
  W_tilde(d,t) := W(d,t)/d removes the d -> 0+ boundary-layer degeneracy in the
  Speiser-Hinkkanen-Lagarias positivity criterion. Combining a division-free Wigner-hyperbolic
  integral representation governed by sinc_hyp(dy) = sinh(dy)/(dy) >= 1, closed-form
  Cauchy-Riemann identities for the higher transverse dipole invariants c_{2m-1}(t) and
  non-singular partial derivatives, and dual directed-rounding interval evaluators (mpmath.iv)
  based on Euler-Maclaurin summation and Jacobi-theta quadrature, we establish strict
  positivity c_1(gamma_k), c_3(gamma_k), c_5(gamma_k) > 0 across the first ten non-trivial
  zeros and certify the absence of off-critical zeros across 4,987,101 continuum cells
  covering [0, 0.50] x [0, 55].
